---
source: crates/observed_macros_impl/tests/expansion.rs
expression: output
---
---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[info] #[warning] struct Subject { #[unredacted] v: u64 }

---- yields ----
only one log-severity attribute (`#[trace]`, `#[debug]`, `#[info]`, `#[warning]`, `#[error]`, `#[fatal]`) is allowed

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[info(bogus = "x")] struct Subject { #[unredacted] v: u64 }

---- yields ----
unknown log option `bogus`; expected `name`

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[info = "x"] struct Subject { #[unredacted] v: u64 }

---- yields ----
a log-severity attribute takes an optional message string and `name = "..."`, not `= value`

---- input ----
#[event("e")]
#[info(name = "a", name = "b")] struct Subject { #[unredacted] v: u64 }

---- yields ----
duplicate `name` setting
